SOAPBOX: Wow conditions were amazing this year, however Murphy visited
SOAPBOX: just when things were getting interesting!
SOAPBOX: I was pleased when setting things up this year I had no real
SOAPBOX: problems with equipment, even after an upgrade last month to
SOAPBOX: Win11 everything was right with the world!
SOAPBOX: Everything started well and as lots have mentioned the bands
SOAPBOX: were in great shape. Even my least favourite band (40m) seemed
SOAPBOX: to be kind to me and my new delta-loop for that band worked well.
SOAPBOX: 10m was on fire and it reminded me of when I was first licensed
SOAPBOX: 37 years ago and I thought the band would always be like that Hi!
SOAPBOX: However Murphy was biding his time. Unfortunately for a couple
SOAPBOX: of weeks prior to the contest I had been pretty busy at work
SOAPBOX: which had obviously taken more of a toll than I realised.
SOAPBOX: By 16:00 Sunday I was struggling to know how to work my station
SOAPBOX: so decided to take a break to recover and set my alarm for
SOAPBOX: 1.5hrs...
SOAPBOX: I came to at 23:45 still sitting in-front of the radio with
SOAPBOX: headphones on... I can tell you much bad language followed!
SOAPBOX: I am blaming work, my XYL says its age but that can't be true?
SOAPBOX: Still I made my best score ever, trying to be positive and
SOAPBOX: ignore I might have beaten my Country record...
SOAPBOX: Could'a/would'a/should'a ZZZZzzzzzzz
